    "faq10q": "How do I put my miner into bootloader mode?",
    "faq10a": "Bootloader recovery depends on the hardware. For Bitaxe and NerdAxe, hold BOOT, press and release RESET while continuing to hold BOOT, then release BOOT. BitForge Nano uses automatic USB bootloader entry and should not be opened. For the NerdNOS LilyGO screen, unplug USB, hold the lower-right button, reconnect USB while continuing to hold it, then release the button. Use these recovery steps only if normal flashing does not start.",
    "faq11q": "What does the Mujina beta support?",
    "faq11a": "The Mujina beta uses WebUSB to flash a user-selected Avalon Nano 3S K230 .kdimg image to SPI NAND after checking its structure and every partition SHA-256. Solo Satoshi does not provide or authenticate the image, and an interrupted full-NAND replacement can require recovery. For Bitaxe Gamma Mujina bridge firmware, use Advanced with a merged ESP32-S3 .bin built for address 0x0.",
