    "faq13q": "What happens after an ESP firmware image is written?",
    "faq13a": "After the write is verified, the flasher sends the reset signal and releases its serial connection. This completes the reset sequence, but does not confirm a successful boot. Keep power connected and check the device display or web dashboard to confirm normal operation.",
    "faq14q": "What is sent when I report an issue?",
    "faq14a": "The reply email and description you enter are sent to Solo Satoshi support. The email is used only to respond about that report and is not added to a marketing list or separate flasher contact database. A security provider processes ordinary request data for rate limiting and bot protection, and an email provider delivers and stores the support email. Never include passwords, Wi-Fi credentials, private keys, seed phrases, or other sensitive information.",
    "nanoSupportTitle": "Avalon Nano 3S",
    "nanoSupportText": "Beta WebUSB support for user-supplied K230 .kdimg images. The tool replaces the complete SPI NAND image; Solo Satoshi does not provide or authenticate the firmware.",
    "analyticsPreferences": "Analytics preferences",
    "analyticsTitle": "Optional analytics",
    "analyticsDescription": "We use optional, cookieless analytics to understand visits and tool usage, identify problems, and improve your experience. This does not include support-form text, firmware files, or USB data. Flashing works whether analytics is on or off.",
